***conformance tests***

# regular-module
Parsing the module `regular_plain_source.plain`:
```
***definitions***

***implementation reqs***

- First implementation requirement.
- Second implementation requirement.

***functional specs***

# display-hello-world
Display "hello, world"
```
gives the tree {`definitions`: [], `implementation reqs`: [{markdown `- First implementation requirement.`}, {markdown `- Second implementation requirement.`}], `functional specs`: [{id `display-hello-world`, markdown `Display "hello, world"`, linked_resources [], conformance_tests [], acceptance_tests []}]}.

# comment-lines-are-dropped
The same module with a comment line `> First implementation requirement is a comment.` in place of the first item, and another comment line before `***definitions***`, gives `implementation reqs` [{markdown `- Second implementation requirement.`}].

# indented-comment-lines-are-dropped
The regular module with indented comment lines `  > a comment` between the items gives the same tree as without them.

***acceptance tests***

# invalid-frontmatter
Parsing a text whose frontmatter is `module: [` raises `PlainSyntaxError` whose message starts with `Plain syntax error: Invalid frontmatter: `.
